<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen over parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Tuesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   10.2</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     7.6</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   3.6</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  3.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		4.5</p>
<p>    Norton		    7.5</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0.5</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   4</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department said showers accompanied by thunder will be experienced at a number of places in the Western, Southern, and Sabaragamuwa provinces and Galle and Matara districts. Thundershowers will develop at a few places in the Uva, Northcentral and Eastern provinces during afternon and evening.</p>
</text>
